<p>The local doco series tells the true stories of real people living in un=
ique or diverse circumstances. The selected show is a 45-minute intimate ac=
count of Tui Taurua's journey into empowerment. Tui spent more than two dec=
ades in and out of psychiatric hospitals because of the way the Western len=
s viewed the voices she was hearing in her head.</p>

<p>The following questions are a starting point for reflection. Head to the=
 Forum, which you can find at the top of your Module 1 menu, to add to the =
discussion in the <strong>1.2.6 Document analysis </strong>thread.</p>

<ul><li>What emotions have surfaced when you watch this doco?</li>
	<li>How does the Western worldview differ to M=C4=81ori worldview when it =
comes to 'hearing voices'?</li>
	<li>What M=C4=81ori health model was mentioned that has helped Tui look at=
 her situation differently?</li>
</ul><p>You will need to <a href=3D"https://login.tech.tvnz.co.nz/registrat=
ion" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">sign up to TVNZ On Deman=
d</a> to watch the series.</p>
