<h3>End of Topic</h3>

<p>Ka pai temahi! Good work! You have now completed the topic Te Tiriti o W=
aitangi and M=C4=81ori Health.</p>

<p>In this topic we have explored the significance of Te Tiriti o Waitangi =
in addressing the health disparities experienced by M=C4=81ori. We revisite=
d the history and contents of the treaty and examined the language translat=
ion issues that have led to conflicts and debates about its interpretation.=
 We have examined the development of treaty principles and discussed how th=
ese principles serve as a framework in the health sector and how they can b=
e applied to the everyday practice of support workers. We have also explore=
d the concepts of equity in healthcare and what health inequities look like=
 for people in Aotearoa New Zealand.</p>

<p>With this learning, we move forward to our next topic, where we examine =
the development of the health system in our country.</p>

<p>Haere tonu, ka pai!- great work, keep going!</p>
